  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe problem is to find a step function h on [0, 2] that minimizes the maximum overlap integral C\u2085. This is a non-convex optimization problem due to the bilinear terms in the overlap sums. The plan combines global and local search strategies:\n\na) Use Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) for global exploration to escape local optima\nb) Switch to L-BFGS-B local optimization for exploitation\nc) Maintain feasibility with a repair mechanism\nd) Use initial_h_values as a warm start\ne) Periodically perturb solutions to explore new regions\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nWe represent h as n_points variables h_i \u2208 [0, 1] with sum(h_i) = n_points / 2. The objective is:\n\nC\u2085 = max_{|k| < n_points} [sum_{i=0}^{n_points-1 - |k|} h_i (1 - h_{i+k})] * dx\n\nSubject to:\n- 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1\n- sum(h_i) = n_points / 2\n\nThe problem is non-convex due to h_i h_{i+k} terms.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na) Initialization\n- If initial_h_values exists, use it as starting point\n- Otherwise, initialize particles randomly\n\nb) PSO global search\n- Use inertia, cognitive, and social components\n- Periodically perturb particles to prevent stagnation\n- Maintain personal and global best solutions\n\nc) Local refinement with L-BFGS-B\n- Use best PSO solution as initial guess\n- Compute numerical gradient focusing on dominant lag\n- Apply repair after each iteration\n\nd) Repair function\n- Clip values to [0, 1]\n- Adjust sum to n_points / 2 by redistributing excess/deficit\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Swarm size: 100 particles\n- Initial n_points: 100\n- Local search frequency: every 50 iterations\n- Perturbation rate: 10% of particles every 100 iterations\n- L-BFGS-B parameters: max iterations 100, tolerance 1e-6\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Global search: 80% of budget\n- Local refinement: 20% of budget\n- Track elapsed time in each phase\n- Return best solution found so far\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Ensure 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1\n- Verify sum(h_i) = n_points / 2\n- Recompute C\u2085 using numpy.correlate\n- Check against initial_h_values if available\n- Handle floating point precision issues\n\nThis approach balances exploration and exploitation, leveraging PSO's global search and L-BFGS-B's local refinement while maintaining feasibility through the repair mechanism.",
